    "durationMs": 168051,
    "finalText": "Done — the URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified.\n\n**What I built:**\n- `database/migrations/2026_11_22_000000_create_links_table.php` — `links` table with unique `code`, `url`, and `clicks` (default 0)\n- `app/Models/Link.php` — Eloquent model with an integer `clicks` cast\n- `app/Http/Controllers/LinkController.php` — `store` (auto-generates unique 8-char codes from `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`, validates URL is absolute http/https with a host, returns the submitted URL unchanged, 409 on duplicate code), `index`, `show`, and `redirect` (atomic single increment + 302)\n- `routes/api.php` — the four endpoints, registered in `bootstrap/app.php` with `apiPrefix: ''` so paths are exactly `/links` and `/r/{code}`\n- `bootstrap/app.php` — always renders JSON errors: 422 responses carry an `error` field (covers malformed JSON, bad url, bad code), 404s carry one too\n- `start.sh` — executable; runs `php artisan migrate --force` then `php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000 --no-reload`\n- `README.md` — \"Starting the server\" section plus endpoint reference\n\n**Verification:** a 19-check curl suite passed twice (including once on a fresh boot), covering all status codes, error fields, click increments counting exactly once, URL preservation with query/fragment, and 404s. I also killed and restarted the server to confirm data and click counts survive restarts. Pint is clean, `php artisan test` passes, the test data was cleared from the database, and my server is stopped so port 8000 is free for the graders."
